WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:03.269
-It is time for
"Tonight Show Hashtags"!

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:04.604
-♪ Hashtags ♪

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:07.607
♪♪

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:09.475
♪ Hashtags ♪

00:00:09.475 --> 00:00:12.145
♪♪

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:14.714
-We do this thing every week
where I send out a hashtag

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:17.083
and ask you guys to respond
to that topic.

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:19.118
With Halloween coming up,
I started a hashtag called

00:00:19.118 --> 00:00:21.221 line:0%
#NewHalloweenTraditions.

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:23.256 line:0%
And I asked you guys to tweet
out some new ideas

00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:25.825 line:0%
for Halloween that are
more appropriate for 2020.

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:27.360 line:0%
Within minutes,
it was a trending topic,

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.896
so thank you for playing along,
everyone.

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:31.831
Now I thought I'd share
some of my favorite

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:35.168
new Halloween traditions
responses from you guys.

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:39.305
This first one is from
@changethebee.

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:40.974
B-E-E.

00:00:40.974 --> 00:00:42.274
-[ Buzzing ]

00:00:42.274 --> 00:00:43.843
Change the Bee.

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:45.545
-Wow.
-Hmm.

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:47.547
Um...

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:48.814
like Chance the Rapper.

00:00:48.814 --> 00:00:49.915
-Oh, yeah.

00:00:49.915 --> 00:00:51.183
-Change the Bee.
-Change the bee.

00:00:51.183 --> 00:00:52.252
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:55.388
-A bee whose name is Change.

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:56.656
-Yep.
-Yep.

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:58.290
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:00.693
-She says...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:02.127
"Putting on
your costume and realizing

00:01:02.127 --> 00:01:04.230
it's the first time
you've used a zipper all year."

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:07.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:09.601
Ah...

00:01:09.601 --> 00:01:12.872
This one's from @kblancf.

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.807
She says, "A black cat
crossing your path

00:01:14.807 --> 00:01:17.076
is now good luck because it
means you went outside at least

00:01:17.076 --> 00:01:19.312
once this week."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:21.147
Got to get the steps in, man.

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:23.983
This one is from @kemitorano.

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:26.652
She says, "Dyeing
hand sanitizer red

00:01:26.652 --> 00:01:29.021
to make the kids wash
their hands in 'ghoul's blood'

00:01:29.021 --> 00:01:30.523
before each house."

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:32.058
[ Laughter ]
That's good idea.

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:35.194
-Yeah, that's a great idea.
-I like that. Yeah.

00:01:35.194 --> 00:01:38.598
This one's from
@Andwejigglelike.

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:41.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:44.804
She says, "Instead of dressing
up as zombies, we all dress up

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:47.206
as ourselves because it's pretty
much the same thing now."

00:01:47.206 --> 00:01:50.042
[ Laughter ]
Easy costume.

00:01:50.042 --> 00:01:52.311
This one's from @ghost7.

00:01:52.311 --> 00:01:54.547
They say, "This year's
group costume --

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:57.349
person, woman, man,
camera, TV."

00:01:57.349 --> 00:01:58.551
[ Laughter ]
[ Applause ]

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:00.353
That's --

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:03.389
That's the winner right there.
-Yeah.

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:07.327
-This one's from
@Krystal-Pistil.

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:08.962
She says, "Candy cigarettes

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:10.663
because even the kids
are stressed."

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:13.332
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.332 --> 00:02:17.436
Come on guys, let's put together
one more puzzle.

00:02:17.436 --> 00:02:21.407
This one's from @BrianSamelson.

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:23.409
-Wow.
-Wow. Straight up.

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:24.710
-Yeah.

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:27.146
-That was the one I had
the hardest reading.

00:02:27.146 --> 00:02:28.581
Just his name.
-A real name, right.

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:30.316
-Brian Samelson.

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:33.152
-For me it was
"And we jiggle like."

00:02:33.152 --> 00:02:37.022
'Cause I was thinking, like,
is it that they "jiggle Ike"?

00:02:37.022 --> 00:02:39.292
Like, it's a guy named Ike
and, you know people --

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:41.894
-Oh, no, "And we jiggle like."
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:41.894 --> 00:02:44.664
-Yeah, but I thought it would be
like Brian Samuelson.

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:46.266
-Yeah.
-Brian Samuelson.

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:48.134
-Yeah, but it's not.
-It's Brian Samelson.

00:02:48.134 --> 00:02:50.636
-Yeah, Samelson, just to
throw you off a little bit.

00:02:50.636 --> 00:02:52.772
-Yeah, Brian Sameson.

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:54.439
[ Laughter ]
-Sammy.

00:02:54.439 --> 00:02:56.309
-Sammy.
-Yeah.

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:58.477
-Son.
-Well, maybe...

00:02:58.477 --> 00:02:59.812
-That's all your words.

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:02.982
-...it's Brian Sames,
and then that's his son.

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:04.083
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:06.485
-That's Brian Sammy's son?
-Yeah.

00:03:06.485 --> 00:03:09.522
-Yeah.
-Wow.

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:11.256
That's amazing.
-Yeah.

00:03:11.256 --> 00:03:13.192
You got to think, man.

00:03:13.192 --> 00:03:16.462
-We got a good one.
This is from Brian Samelson.

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:18.330
-No, Brian.

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:20.499
-Sammy's son.
-Who's Brian? Sammy's son.

00:03:20.499 --> 00:03:22.368
-Oh, I got you. Yeah, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:23.903
-This is from Sammy's son.

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:25.638
-Yeah, it's from Sammy's son,
Brian.

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:29.241
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.241 --> 00:03:31.077
-He says,
"New 'Peanuts' special --

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:33.112
'It's a Rapid Test,
Charlie Brown.'"

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:37.016
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:38.818
Only available on Apple TV+.

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:42.388
[ Laughter ]
-Ah!

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:44.857
This last one is from
@atarikari.

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:46.693
Cool.
She says, "Trick or treat,

00:03:46.693 --> 00:03:49.662
stay 6 feet, throw me candy
from the street."

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:50.929
There you go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:50.929 --> 00:03:53.232
That's a good bop.
That slaps.

00:03:53.232 --> 00:03:55.001
There you have it. Those are our
"Tonight Show Hashtags."

00:03:55.001 --> 00:03:56.335 line:0%
To check out more of our
favorites go to

00:03:56.335 --> 00:03:59.105 line:0%
tonightshow.com/hashtags.

